# Dropbox and Windows leave these behind in every folder they touch.
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store
*conflicted copy*
~$*

__pycache__/
*.pyc

# internal/ is NOT ignored, on purpose.
#
# It holds internal/costs.json and the supplier catalogues the generator reads,
# so leaving it out would make this repository unable to rebuild itself - the
# backup would be incomplete in the one way that matters.
#
# It carries dealer cost. That is safe here and nowhere else:
#   - this repository is PRIVATE
#   - internal/ is never deployed; the site is served from the root files only
#   - no cost ever enters assets/js/data.js, which browsers download
#
# If this repository is ever made public, internal/ has to come out first,
# and out of the history, not just the working tree.
